## Finding (issue #74 "win or match always", lossless graphics)
The lossless-graphics gap vs cjxl is HETEROGENEOUS and correlates with
background dominance (top_color_pct):
  - top_color_pct > ~80% (sparse, background-dominant docs) -> we LOSE
    (5336 +26.1%, 5340 +6.1%, 5342 +9.2%, 8432 +25.5%)
  - lower dominance -> we WIN/match (5334 -52.9%, 5324 -25.0%)
  - palette-friendly (few unique colors) -> we WIN big (8222: 499 colors, -68.1%)
  - dense photos -> match (+0.2..+0.4%)

## Ruled-out levers (measured 2026-07-14, do not re-try without new evidence)
  - Context-map ANS+LZ77 writer: ALREADY at libjxl parity
    (write_context_map_nonsimple picks Huffman+MTF vs ANS+LZ77 by cost).
  - ANS histogram cap 128 -> 256: NO effect (clustering already picks the
    cost-optimal count <=128; CLUSTERS_LIMIT is already 256).
  - Global tree-threshold multiplier (JXL_TREE_THRESH_MUL sweep 1x..32x):
    helps ONLY the 5336 outlier (255415 -> 193898 at 8x, -24%), while
    regressing photos monotonically (+0.4% -> +3.3% at 32x) and NOT helping
    other sparse docs (5340/5342 monotonically prefer the big 1x tree).
  - Trial-encode two tree sizes, keep smaller: measured LOW-EV
    (1/13 images improved, by ~1pp) — NOT worth the 2x tree-learn cost.

## Root cause (attribution, 5336 e7: ours 255415 vs cjxl 202517, +26.1%)
  LfGlobal (global MA tree): ours 10904 B (2059 nodes / 1030 ctx / 128 histo)
                             vs cjxl 312 B (tiny tree). +10592 B / +3395%.
  GroupPass (residuals):     ours 244229 vs cjxl 201912. +42317 B / +21%.
  The big tree over-splits on sparse content (removed threshold floor won
  CLIC photos -0.7% but over-splits documents) AND codes residuals WORSE.
  No single global knob fixes it; needs content-adaptive tree regularization
  OR a better modular predictor/context model on high-background-dominance
  content. A zenanalyze-proxy discriminator can PREDICT the loss
  (top_color_pct) but there is no alternative modular strategy that WINS
  these cells to route to (unlike the lossy Libjxl<->Zenjxl choice).

## cjxl PNG-read robustness
cjxl v0.11.2 fails ("Getting pixel data failed") on some Display-P3 / Android
EXIF PNGs (e.g. 8025 mobile screenshot) and produces NO output. Naive sweeps
that stat() a reused temp path then compare against a STALE previous output
(observed: a bogus 8025 "+265%" that was actually the prior image's cjxl size).
This harness records such cells as cjxl_fail and never compares them.
Scoreboard cjxl-dominant counts should be filtered for this contamination.
